{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"CHANGE 1344 IS UP BUT BLOCKED ON BOTH GATES, AND THE BLOCK IS CHEAP TO CLEAR. Read this before touching the code — the code is probably fine.\n\nhttps://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1344 -- LLM-Review = -1, Verified = -1.\n\nTHE LLM-Review BLOCK IS NOT A CODE FINDING. Verbatim: \"(bugfix-size-attestation) this change touches 554 non-test line(s) - over the 150-line floor for a bug fix - but bug 129e-2d88-cce2-492c has no acceptable plan-review attestation (verdict: unsigned; no plan-review attestation record)\". So the gate wants a certified plan review on THIS ticket because the fix is large, exactly as the debug protocol warns for a fix whose blast radius reaches non-test code.\n\nAND THE ATTESTATION ALREADY EXISTS - IT IS MERELY STALE. rebar review-plan 129e --status returns verdict \"stale-head\": signed at 5bc3a432d7 while HEAD has moved on. A plan review was run on this ticket earlier today and returned PASS with 0 blocking. So the first thing to try is rebar sign-review 129e-2d88-cce2-492c, which RE-SIGNS FROM THE RECORDED REVIEW WITH NO LLM SPEND. Only pay for a fresh review-plan if that refuses. Then re-push or comment recheck on 1344.\n\nTHE Verified -1 IS UNDIAGNOSED and must not be assumed to be a real test failure. Today's identical-looking failure on another change was the STALE-BASE TRAP: Gerrit CI runs the TARGET branch's workflow against the patchset's tree, so a gate script added to main after the change was based fails on a missing file. 1344 was based on 5bc3a432d7 and main has advanced several times since. CHECK FOR THAT FIRST - rebase onto current origin/main and re-push - before reading the failure as a defect in the change.\n\nWHAT THE CHANGE CONTAINS, per the implementer's report: _anthropic_web_search_capabilities is deleted from anthropic_model.py and replaced by web_search_capabilities(*, web: bool) in capabilities.py, taking NO model or provider argument at all, so it cannot gate on a name shape. One WebSearch(native=WebSearchTool(max_uses=5), local=duckduckgo_search_tool(max_results=5)). New profile-derived ModelCapabilities.native_web_search read by MEMBERSHIP in supported_native_tools. provider_provenance.capabilities.web_access records \"native\" | \"local\" | \"off\". The duckduckgo group was folded into the agents extra itself so no deployment can install the agents runtime and forget it; uv.lock regenerated. Full suite 9863 passed.\n\nA TRAP THE IMPLEMENTER FOUND THAT MUST NOT BE UNDONE: setting max_uses / blocked_domains / allowed_domains at the CAPABILITY level flips pydantic-ai's _requires_native() to True, and NativeOrLocalTool.get_toolset() then returns None - which SUPPRESSES the local fallback and hard-fails on any provider lacking the native tool. That is the original bug re-created. max_uses therefore rides the NATIVE TOOL INSTANCE, and a test asserts get_toolset() is not None. Do not \"harden\" the capability by moving those kwargs up a level.\n\nSTILL OWED ON THIS TICKET: AC2 asks for verification by a RUN on each configured provider. What exists is the attach path exercised per provider through the runner plus the route read off each real profile - no live model call. A live Bedrock plan-review showing web_access \"local\" on a signed verdict would close it outright."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785818123816691001,"uuid":"62d52a56-ac8c-4b6c-a7e3-17bd744dcb71"}